# Production environment — baked into the React bundle at build time.
#
# ── Option A: Vercel proxy (current default) ────────────────────────────────
# Leave REACT_APP_API_URL empty so axios uses relative paths (/api/…).
# The Vercel serverless proxy (api/[...path].js) intercepts every /api/*
# request and forwards it to the backend, eliminating CORS and mixed-content
# issues entirely.  Update BACKEND_HOST in api/[...path].js to point at your
# Railway service URL after deployment.
#
# ── Option B: Direct Railway calls (CORS-enabled) ───────────────────────────
# Uncomment the line below and replace the placeholder with your actual
# Railway service URL to bypass the Vercel proxy entirely.
# Railway must have ALLOWED_ORIGINS set to your Vercel deployment URL so the
# browser's CORS pre-flight check passes.
#
# REACT_APP_API_URL=https://YOUR-RAILWAY-APP.up.railway.app
#
# ── Active setting ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Using Option A (Vercel proxy) by default — REACT_APP_API_URL is intentionally
# empty.  To switch to direct Railway calls, comment out the line below and
# uncomment the Option B line above with your real Railway URL.
REACT_APP_API_URL=
